WEBVTT

00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:09.670
Explosive Shoot

00:00:16.490 --> 00:00:19.810
Keep fighting chasing your dream

00:00:19.810 --> 00:00:23.140
with love, courage and friendship

00:00:23.140 --> 00:00:26.640
This Blade and I are one

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:29.680
Spin as hard as you can until the limit

00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:32.780
BURNING SOUL

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:46.200
The things I can't do alone

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:50.140
are not impossible if you're with me

00:00:50.490 --> 00:00:52.960
Come with me

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:56.280
to the ends of this world

00:00:58.070 --> 00:01:03.540
The Four Sacred Beasts are athletes of love

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:07.100
Shine! Open your eyes!

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:09.730
Dragoon  Dranzer  Draciel  Driger

00:01:09.730 --> 00:01:12.450
Awaken!

00:01:12.790 --> 00:01:16.060
Fly across the sky, my energy

00:01:16.060 --> 00:01:19.380
Rise up, Sacred Beast!

00:01:19.380 --> 00:01:22.830
To defeat all the enemies who stand in our way

00:01:22.830 --> 00:01:26.050
jump, bearing everyone's hopes

00:01:26.070 --> 00:01:29.080
SHINING SOUL

00:02:42.260 --> 00:02:45.490
No good. With his speed, he's sure to hit me.

00:02:46.210 --> 00:02:47.400
Takao!

00:02:47.840 --> 00:02:50.160
What are you doing out here?

00:02:50.160 --> 00:02:52.090
Oh, Professor.

00:02:52.090 --> 00:02:53.410
I couldn't sleep.

00:02:56.360 --> 00:02:59.410
You're trying to come up with a
way to beat Giancarlo, I assume.

00:02:59.700 --> 00:03:02.550
Yep. I still wanna fight him again.

00:03:03.060 --> 00:03:05.660
I need to beat him no matter what!

00:03:06.060 --> 00:03:08.730
So, have you devised a suitable strategy?

00:03:09.010 --> 00:03:10.750
Heh, I wish.

00:03:10.750 --> 00:03:15.090
I'm picturing all kinds of scenarios,
but I can't seem to come up with a good one.

00:03:15.570 --> 00:03:17.800
That's what we're here for, you know.

00:03:18.160 --> 00:03:19.770
Rei! Max!

00:03:19.770 --> 00:03:22.030
So uncool, Takao.

00:03:22.030 --> 00:03:24.160
We can help you find a way.

00:03:24.160 --> 00:03:26.680
Then let's devise a strategy together.

00:03:27.220 --> 00:03:28.530
You guys..!

00:03:31.200 --> 00:03:36.190
Defeat Amphisbaena

00:03:42.560 --> 00:03:45.950
Let's start by analyzing the situation of our battle.

00:03:47.290 --> 00:03:50.940
Giancarlo's trademark move is the Twin Destruction.

00:03:50.940 --> 00:03:54.950
It's a two-phase attack that
makes use of Amphisbaena's two heads.

00:03:55.660 --> 00:03:58.340
Both its speed and power are off the charts.

00:03:58.340 --> 00:04:01.430
Yeah. It's not something I can easily brush off.

00:04:01.430 --> 00:04:04.320
If only I could stop his Sacred Beast from moving.

00:04:04.800 --> 00:04:08.250
Still, it is quite hot-blooded!

00:04:08.250 --> 00:04:12.730
Giancarlo must be a truly skilled Blader
to be able to control a Sacred Beast that easily.

00:04:13.060 --> 00:04:15.390
He's got a big ego, too.

00:04:15.390 --> 00:04:17.500
Maybe... we could make use of that?

00:04:18.570 --> 00:04:22.780
Giancarlo has complete confidence
in his ability to control his Sacred Beast.

00:04:22.780 --> 00:04:25.500
But over-confidence leads to carelessness.

00:04:25.980 --> 00:04:30.750
By exploiting that, we may be
able to stop his Sacred Beast's attack.

00:04:31.330 --> 00:04:34.000
Exploiting it, huh..?

00:04:34.220 --> 00:04:36.730
Ah, that's an interesting idea.

00:04:36.980 --> 00:04:38.180
That's it..!

00:04:38.180 --> 00:04:39.420
Jeez, you scared me!

00:04:39.610 --> 00:04:43.160
Please don't be so quick to raise your voice!
We're in the dead of night, you know.

00:04:43.550 --> 00:04:47.410
<i>Sorry, sorry.</i> So what do you think of this plan?

00:04:47.410 --> 00:04:48.400
What plan?

00:04:48.400 --> 00:04:50.420
Well, you see, <i>whisper, whisper</i>...

00:04:57.730 --> 00:04:59.950
How did you come up with such a strategy?!

00:05:00.350 --> 00:05:02.880
Still, it's simple and to the point.

00:05:02.880 --> 00:05:06.020
Kind of dumb, but I think it can work.

00:05:06.020 --> 00:05:07.880
Max, I'm on board!

00:05:07.880 --> 00:05:10.280
Alright! So it's a deal, then.

00:05:10.280 --> 00:05:12.890
Professor, you take care of Dragoon.

00:05:13.140 --> 00:05:14.970
Very well.

00:05:24.500 --> 00:05:25.700
Here, Takao.

00:05:25.700 --> 00:05:27.390
Huh? You're already finished?

00:05:27.730 --> 00:05:32.150
Yep! I only needed to make some minor tweaks for our fight with Amphisbaena.

00:05:32.540 --> 00:05:35.520
Alright. Guess it's time to give it a spin!

00:05:38.940 --> 00:05:40.530
Go Shoot!

00:05:47.420 --> 00:05:50.260
Mm-hm. It's all following my calculations.

00:05:50.260 --> 00:05:56.770
These swift movements were made possible thanks to an
ingenious combination of a new Spin Gear and Blade Base.

00:05:57.020 --> 00:06:00.640
This should have Max's plan go off without a hitch.

00:06:00.640 --> 00:06:01.340
<i>Yes!</i>

00:06:07.790 --> 00:06:09.650
Now things are looking interesting!

00:06:09.650 --> 00:06:11.950
Don't get complacent just yet.

00:06:11.950 --> 00:06:15.950
We still need to improve the speed of your jumps.

00:06:16.210 --> 00:06:18.650
Takao, it all rests on today's training.

00:06:19.000 --> 00:06:20.370
Okay!

00:06:21.460 --> 00:06:23.500
You won't get any speed with that stance.

00:06:24.670 --> 00:06:25.530
Kai!

00:06:26.550 --> 00:06:30.030
Try to angle the Bey a bit more as you shoot.

00:06:30.030 --> 00:06:31.750
Angle the Bey?

00:06:32.050 --> 00:06:33.170
Alright.

00:06:33.550 --> 00:06:35.080
Go Shoot!

00:06:38.730 --> 00:06:40.760
Oh, it's faster than before!

00:06:42.680 --> 00:06:45.300
Awesome! Thanks, Kai.

00:06:47.340 --> 00:06:51.230
You guys, too.
You've helped me come up with a solution.

00:06:51.620 --> 00:06:53.760
You can thank us later.

00:06:53.760 --> 00:06:55.650
For now, you need to focus on training.

00:06:56.850 --> 00:06:59.170
Alright... You wait, Giancarlo!

00:06:59.170 --> 00:07:01.600
This time, I <i>will</i> beat you!

00:07:06.580 --> 00:07:09.630
Are you really going to buy us clothes, Giancarlo?

00:07:09.860 --> 00:07:12.920
Yes, of course! Grab all the clothes you want.

00:07:13.140 --> 00:07:15.200
Awesome! I'm glad!

00:07:15.200 --> 00:07:16.690
Hey, are you seeing this?

00:07:16.690 --> 00:07:17.790
Which one?

00:07:17.790 --> 00:07:19.300
Look! It's gorgeous!

00:07:34.910 --> 00:07:36.120
Seiryuu...

00:07:38.330 --> 00:07:39.650
True, I did beat him...

00:07:40.430 --> 00:07:43.800
so why am I so unsatisfied?

00:07:44.410 --> 00:07:47.070
Something inside of me is still irked by it.

00:07:47.370 --> 00:07:49.500
What's wrong? You're just standing there...

00:07:50.280 --> 00:07:52.170
Oh, it's nothing.

00:07:52.170 --> 00:07:53.820
Shall we go into the store?

00:07:53.820 --> 00:07:54.560
Yeah!

00:07:54.560 --> 00:07:55.460
Okay then.

00:07:59.600 --> 00:08:00.800
It's been a while, hasn't it?

00:08:01.430 --> 00:08:02.810
Olivier!

00:08:06.660 --> 00:08:09.170
Sorry for barging on your date.

00:08:09.490 --> 00:08:12.210
Don't be sorry. I did buy the clothes I promised.

00:08:12.400 --> 00:08:15.100
Plus, you came all the way from France to see me.

00:08:15.300 --> 00:08:17.020
How could I outright ignore you?

00:08:17.230 --> 00:08:22.830
Yet it's a shame... I hoped to witness your
battle with Kinomiya, but it appears I'm too late.

00:08:23.050 --> 00:08:26.060
Regardless, I knew you'd come out on top.

00:08:27.270 --> 00:08:28.790
Yeah, I guess so.

00:08:29.050 --> 00:08:32.780
What's wrong? Sounds like something's on your mind.

00:08:33.250 --> 00:08:35.290
Actually, something is bothering me.

00:08:35.470 --> 00:08:36.900
Bothering you?

00:08:36.900 --> 00:08:43.850
My Bey's performance, my ability as a Blader—
I essentially beat him out in all departments.

00:08:44.250 --> 00:08:45.800
As such, that's why I was able to win.

00:08:46.450 --> 00:08:51.930
Even then, I feel like he possesses
some sort of attribute that we lack.

00:08:52.170 --> 00:08:53.440
Like what?

00:08:54.050 --> 00:08:56.500
It can't be put into words.

00:08:57.480 --> 00:08:59.610
Are you sure you're not just imagining it?

00:09:00.730 --> 00:09:01.940
You may be right.

00:09:02.260 --> 00:09:06.960
Take me, for example. Our battle
ended in a very hideous fashion—a tie.

00:09:06.960 --> 00:09:10.020
But I think there was a reason for that.

00:09:10.360 --> 00:09:12.860
I didn't put in quite enough effort.

00:09:13.120 --> 00:09:14.160
Effort?

00:09:14.380 --> 00:09:19.750
Exactly. An effort born from
believing in yourself, not relying on others.

00:09:21.510 --> 00:09:26.940
Isn't that the reason why we were able to
triumph over all kinds of Bladers up to now?

00:09:27.350 --> 00:09:29.840
Like how I beat the Austrian, Cadav.

00:09:34.470 --> 00:09:37.010
And you defeated Phan of Egypt.

00:09:41.150 --> 00:09:46.160
You're right. All I need to do is
seize victory by believing in myself.

00:09:46.500 --> 00:09:50.410
I guess I was overthinking things.

00:09:50.720 --> 00:09:52.900
Indeed. This is not like you at all.

00:09:53.470 --> 00:09:54.700
Truthfully, yeah.

00:10:00.780 --> 00:10:04.580
You came all the way to Rome.
You can sleep at my place tonight.

00:10:04.580 --> 00:10:06.370
I think I'll take you up on that offer.

00:10:07.330 --> 00:10:09.170
Great, Takao! That's it!

00:10:17.960 --> 00:10:20.290
Alright! One more time!

00:10:21.530 --> 00:10:22.940
Takao Kinomiya!

00:10:24.340 --> 00:10:25.610
Giancarlo!

00:10:25.610 --> 00:10:26.940
And Olivier, too!

00:10:27.930 --> 00:10:30.700
Takao, what are you doing out here?

00:10:30.700 --> 00:10:31.820
You first.

00:10:32.250 --> 00:10:34.210
We were merely passing by.

00:10:34.420 --> 00:10:35.610
So, how about you?

00:10:35.880 --> 00:10:38.030
Oh, what a coincidence!

00:10:38.280 --> 00:10:40.620
I'm training to defeat you.

00:10:41.000 --> 00:10:42.130
What's that?

00:10:42.310 --> 00:10:44.670
Your battle has already passed, has it not?

00:10:44.950 --> 00:10:50.460
Yeah, that's right. I couldn't really do any
damage... which is exactly why I want a rematch!

00:10:51.010 --> 00:10:52.190
A rematch..?

00:10:52.190 --> 00:10:55.320
Foolish. He's going to win,
no matter how many times you try.

00:10:55.710 --> 00:10:56.730
Say again?!

00:10:57.070 --> 00:11:00.070
Demanding a rematch when the
results are clear as day is a waste of time.

00:11:00.070 --> 00:11:01.610
Now, let us go.

00:11:02.530 --> 00:11:03.630
Wait.

00:11:05.310 --> 00:11:11.490
That attribute I felt... If I fought him
again, I would be able to ascertain its existence.

00:11:11.770 --> 00:11:13.630
You're still hung up on that?

00:11:14.910 --> 00:11:16.790
A bit curious, is all.

00:11:17.170 --> 00:11:20.880
Takao Kinomiya, I accept your challenge.

00:11:20.880 --> 00:11:23.000
Alright, now we're talking!

00:11:23.280 --> 00:11:25.500
As for the time and place...

00:11:25.820 --> 00:11:30.010
Tomorrow morning. That fateful place. Sound good?

00:11:30.370 --> 00:11:32.650
Sure, I'll be there.

00:11:58.830 --> 00:12:01.240
Giancarlo, are you good to go?

00:12:04.200 --> 00:12:04.820
Yeah.

00:12:05.040 --> 00:12:07.060
Do your best, Takao!

00:12:07.060 --> 00:12:08.410
Go for it!

00:12:08.410 --> 00:12:12.370
Professor said he's treating us to dinner if you win!

00:12:12.710 --> 00:12:17.180
Eh?! Now, wait a minute!
I never said anything about that!

00:12:17.760 --> 00:12:19.920
Giancarlo looks serious...

00:12:20.120 --> 00:12:23.940
Truth is, I can't see them possessing something we don't.

00:12:24.570 --> 00:12:28.050
As Olivier said, I'm probably imagining it.

00:12:28.480 --> 00:12:31.920
But I don't like having unfinished business.

00:12:32.770 --> 00:12:36.570
Let us quickly confirm my overthinking!

00:12:38.470 --> 00:12:40.590
I'm not gonna go easy on you!

00:12:41.070 --> 00:12:43.480
Let us begin, Takao Kinomiya!

00:12:47.120 --> 00:12:48.380
Come!

00:12:52.380 --> 00:12:53.200
Three!

00:12:53.630 --> 00:12:54.420
Two!

00:12:54.900 --> 00:12:55.700
One!

00:12:56.600 --> 00:12:58.830
Go... Shoot!

00:12:59.050 --> 00:13:00.770
Go!

00:13:09.300 --> 00:13:11.160
Come forth, Amphisbaena!

00:13:19.020 --> 00:13:20.610
Chew him up!

00:13:23.580 --> 00:13:24.290
What?!

00:13:35.070 --> 00:13:37.330
Oh... A new strategy, is it?

00:13:37.720 --> 00:13:42.300
So long as I'm in command, Amphisbaena won't fall for it!

00:13:42.590 --> 00:13:44.100
Twin Destruction!

00:13:48.170 --> 00:13:49.540
This is good.

00:13:49.850 --> 00:13:51.450
<i>Nice</i>.

00:13:51.450 --> 00:13:53.940
Our speed training is coming to light.

00:13:54.240 --> 00:13:57.820
Giancarlo! How about you try a bit harder?

00:13:57.820 --> 00:13:59.560
You're not keeping up with him!

00:14:00.300 --> 00:14:05.000
Against <i>him</i>? Don't make me laugh. Last
time, I beat him using 60 percent of my power.

00:14:05.000 --> 00:14:06.690
I won't need any more than that!

00:14:11.570 --> 00:14:12.560
What?!

00:14:14.940 --> 00:14:17.830
This is no time for infighting! Quiet yourselves!

00:14:19.060 --> 00:14:20.480
I'm not done yet!

00:14:34.490 --> 00:14:38.230
H-Hey, now! Focus on the battle!
What the heck are you doing?!

00:14:38.560 --> 00:14:40.480
<i>Okay!</i> Everything is going according to plan.

00:14:40.480 --> 00:14:45.400
You were careless, Giancarlo. You shouldn't have
put on airs and used 60 percent of your strength!

00:14:45.680 --> 00:14:51.520
Amphisbaena is hot-blooded. If this situation
persists, you won't be able to control him anymore!

00:14:56.530 --> 00:14:57.840
Amphisbaena!

00:15:00.350 --> 00:15:02.130
Hey! Stop it! Stop it, I said!

00:15:02.770 --> 00:15:05.290
I see..! So this was their goal all along!

00:15:05.480 --> 00:15:06.600
Right on the money.

00:15:07.050 --> 00:15:11.340
By making use of its personality and
having the two heads fight each other,

00:15:11.340 --> 00:15:15.240
they'll ignore Giancarlo's orders, and thus, stop attacking Dragoon!

00:15:15.570 --> 00:15:19.200
It's kind of dumb, but it's simple and to the point.

00:15:19.200 --> 00:15:22.830
And while they're busy fighting
one another, Dragoon can strike!

00:15:25.380 --> 00:15:29.640
Enough! Amphisbaena, why are you ignoring my orders?!

00:15:29.640 --> 00:15:30.500
You idiot!

00:15:36.620 --> 00:15:38.590
Alright! Now's your chance, Dragoon!

00:15:41.190 --> 00:15:43.220
Phantom Hurricane!

00:16:00.350 --> 00:16:01.350
He dodged it?!

00:16:02.010 --> 00:16:03.120
No, that's not it.

00:16:11.550 --> 00:16:12.780
Why you..!

00:16:17.640 --> 00:16:18.580
Giancarlo!

00:16:20.450 --> 00:16:22.510
This is bad. We got him too mad!

00:16:22.510 --> 00:16:23.840
<i>Oh my God!</i>

00:16:24.260 --> 00:16:25.420
Giancarlo!

00:16:25.420 --> 00:16:26.600
Stay there!

00:16:26.600 --> 00:16:27.790
But..!

00:16:29.720 --> 00:16:31.590
That's <i>my</i> Sacred Beast!

00:16:31.970 --> 00:16:35.430
I will calm him down myself!
I don't need anyone else's help!

00:16:35.910 --> 00:16:37.840
Stop, Amphisbaena!

00:16:38.090 --> 00:16:41.700
It's useless! He's completely lost control of himself!

00:16:44.180 --> 00:16:45.500
You must stop!

00:16:45.930 --> 00:16:49.200
I'm your master! Why won't you obey me?

00:16:54.320 --> 00:16:56.200
This is bad. Dragoon!

00:17:06.920 --> 00:17:08.040
Seiryuu?!

00:17:13.550 --> 00:17:15.200
Are you okay, Giancarlo?

00:17:15.200 --> 00:17:16.020
Takao!

00:17:16.370 --> 00:17:21.860
Didn't think he would get this angry.
I promise I'll do something about this.

00:17:26.510 --> 00:17:28.380
Seiyuu got bitten!

00:17:29.150 --> 00:17:30.020
This is bad!

00:17:30.670 --> 00:17:34.240
It's useless. Amphisbaena is much stronger.

00:17:34.240 --> 00:17:37.710
Right now, getting away and
fighting back are out of the question.

00:17:38.260 --> 00:17:41.490
All that's left is to wait and be destroyed.

00:17:42.440 --> 00:17:43.690
Takao!

00:17:43.690 --> 00:17:46.320
There's got to be something... something I can do!

00:17:46.960 --> 00:17:48.080
Wait..!

00:17:48.080 --> 00:17:51.450
Thanks to the Professor,
Dragoon's jumping ability has improved.

00:17:51.810 --> 00:17:55.380
So maybe, just maybe, Seiryu's
ability to jump has improved, too.

00:17:56.080 --> 00:17:59.260
All or nothing! Seiryuu, jump now!

00:18:04.100 --> 00:18:05.070
What?!

00:18:05.070 --> 00:18:08.770
Madness! He jumped while
constricted by Amphisbaena!

00:18:08.770 --> 00:18:10.780
Go high!

00:18:27.500 --> 00:18:30.550
He's still standing? Just how tough is he?!

00:18:55.560 --> 00:18:57.240
End it, Dragoon!

00:18:58.450 --> 00:19:00.960
Phantom Attack!

00:19:23.860 --> 00:19:25.240
You did it!

00:19:25.240 --> 00:19:26.180
Takao!

00:19:26.180 --> 00:19:27.190
He really won!

00:19:31.780 --> 00:19:34.060
You were great, Takao. Good job.

00:19:34.060 --> 00:19:37.100
You had me worried for a moment, but you pulled through.

00:19:37.100 --> 00:19:39.580
Indeed. Our strategy succeeded.

00:19:39.730 --> 00:19:42.360
It was truly <i>very good</i>.

00:19:42.360 --> 00:19:45.820
This is our first victory against
the members of the Euro team.

00:19:45.820 --> 00:19:47.590
Yeah, a win at last!

00:19:47.840 --> 00:19:52.340
Alright! All is well that ends well. Now let's top it off with a tasty dinner!

00:19:52.340 --> 00:19:53.850
Professor's treat, of course.

00:19:53.990 --> 00:19:55.930
W-W-W-Wa-Wait!

00:19:57.790 --> 00:19:58.750
What's wrong?

00:19:59.150 --> 00:20:02.950
I never said anything about that!
It's all something that Max made up!

00:20:02.950 --> 00:20:05.470
Oh, come on! I won and everything!

00:20:05.470 --> 00:20:06.970
Don't be a cheapskate!

00:20:06.970 --> 00:20:09.470
I'm not paying for your dinner! I know how much you eat!

00:20:10.580 --> 00:20:17.400
By making Seiryuu jump, he managed to turn the battle
around. I could never come up with something like that.

00:20:17.930 --> 00:20:19.980
As predicted, there's something to him.

00:20:20.310 --> 00:20:23.240
A potential beyond our imagination.

00:20:24.200 --> 00:20:26.230
I guess I'll have to admit that.

00:20:27.410 --> 00:20:28.320
Takao!

00:20:33.080 --> 00:20:35.080
There's someone I'd like you to meet.

00:20:35.330 --> 00:20:39.130
He's really strong. Ralf, a Blader from Germany.

00:20:39.130 --> 00:20:42.140
Ralf? As in, Ralf Jurngens?!

00:21:04.080 --> 00:21:05.570
You already know him?

00:21:05.570 --> 00:21:07.220
Of course!

00:21:07.220 --> 00:21:08.960
Darn right I know him...

00:21:08.960 --> 00:21:12.090
He's the reason we started our journey through Europe.

00:21:12.690 --> 00:21:14.750
I see, Ralf...

00:21:14.750 --> 00:21:19.520
Oh, well. We can't avoid him at this point, anyway.

00:21:19.520 --> 00:21:22.610
I can finally meet him again...

00:21:39.960 --> 00:21:44.720
Spring waves its hand smiling,

00:21:44.720 --> 00:21:50.200
Summer spreads passion.

00:21:50.200 --> 00:21:55.350
Seasons pass one after the other,

00:21:55.350 --> 00:21:59.560
Fall and Winter are good friends.

00:22:01.000 --> 00:22:05.660
When there is a problem you can't solve,

00:22:05.660 --> 00:22:11.560
Trust, friendship, love and emotion

00:22:14.120 --> 00:22:18.800
Clouds keep flying across the sky,

00:22:18.800 --> 00:22:24.200
the sky keeps changing every second

00:22:24.200 --> 00:22:29.090
My eyes well up and tears stream down my face,

00:22:29.090 --> 00:22:33.090
but they're not tears of sadness

00:22:34.820 --> 00:22:39.420
I summon my courage and try to put it into words.

00:22:39.420 --> 00:22:44.770
"Let's go on a journey to the city of hope!"

00:22:44.770 --> 00:22:49.760
All your dreams will come true

00:22:58.050 --> 00:23:02.740
According to my analysis, our reunion
with Ralf is going to call forth a storm.

00:23:03.310 --> 00:23:08.970
And yet, ignoring Giancarlo's
advice, Ralf rejects Takao's challenge.

00:23:09.420 --> 00:23:14.250
When we were feeling lost, the fourthBlader of the Euro team appeared before us.

00:23:14.250 --> 00:23:16.580
The British Johnny McGregor!

00:23:17.650 --> 00:23:20.410
Next time: The Royal Blader.

00:23:21.220 --> 00:23:23.990
A surprising Bond!
